(4472795, 641084, 81382, '<td valign="top">Don''t really understand this. This is pretty much just a texture with no focal point composed off center thanks to the lighting</td>', 'Don''t really understand this. This is pretty much just a texture with no focal point composed off center thanks to the lighting', '2008-02-09 10:07:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(4472797, 641869, 81382, '<td valign="top">A lot of the brick work detail has been lost in the shadows and there is no detail in the sky at all - overused by some, but here HDR would have been perfect. The connection with the earliest memory isn''t as strong as others</td>', 'A lot of the brick work detail has been lost in the shadows and there is no detail in the sky at all - overused by some, but here HDR would have been perfect. The connection with the earliest memory isn''t as strong as others', '2008-02-09 10:09:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(4472833, 641972, 74559, '<td valign="top">Love the distortion, very fun!</td>', 'Love the distortion, very fun!', '2008-02-09 10:34:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(4472962, 642112, 83080, '<td valign="top">Nice idea.  This really brings back memories.  Such a narrow &amp; well defined DOF is distracting to me here.  I wonder what result you might have gotten by bending back the paper in symmetry with the silly putty so that only the crease between them would plunge into (or out of) the focal plane, then rotate.  The overall composition has nice lines and it''s fun overall.</td>', 'Nice idea.  This really brings back memories.  Such a narrow & well defined DOF is distracting to me here.  I wonder what result you might have gotten by bending back the paper in symmetry with the silly putty so that only the crease between them would plunge into (or out of) the focal plane, then rotate.  The overall composition has nice lines and it''s fun overall.', '2008-02-09 12:45:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(4472987, 641084, 83080, '<td valign="top">It occurs to me that you might get a DNMC score or two since that was my first reaction before thinking about it for a while.  Now this strikes me as quite insightful since most of us probably have an early memory or two of examining light through some type of cloth.<br/> <br/>The texture is deep and rich (like I remember).  There''s a slight right tilt to the grain of the fabric that I wish were either stronger or leveled out.  Good luck and thanks for making me think with this one.</td>', 'It occurs to me that you might get a DNMC score or two since that was my first reaction before thinking about it for a while.  Now this strikes me as quite insightful since most of us probably have an early memory or two of examining light through some type of cloth. The texture is deep and rich (like I remember).  There''s a slight right tilt to the grain of the fabric that I wish were either stronger or leveled out.  Good luck and thanks for making me think with this one.', '2008-02-09 12:58:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(4472990, 641162, 83080, '<td valign="top">Wow, talk about meeting the challenge!  This really brings back memories for me thanks to the way you composed this shot (right down to including those simple cards).  Thanks for the memories :)</td>', 'Wow, talk about meeting the challenge!  This really brings back memories for me thanks to the way you composed this shot (right down to including those simple cards).  Thanks for the memories :)', '2008-02-09 12:58:57.000000', NULL, 1),
